    "tip": "Use Ireland as your example of GDP and GNP differing: GNP is lower than GDP because profits flow out to foreign owners. Do not say Ireland is the richest country in the world, and do not give a dollar figure for Irish GDP per head. Luxembourg's high figure is also inflated, by cross-border commuters, so do not treat either as proof of the highest living standards."
